Regression test for the Chinese catala_zh lexer dialect: Chinese keywords and
yen money literals (comma as thousands grouping, dot as decimal separator),
frozen through typechecking and all four code-generation backends.

Note: user-defined identifiers must currently be ASCII. The zh lexer only
accepts Chinese characters for its built-in keyword, type and constructor names,
because the shared identifier rule matches Unicode upper/lowercase letters plus
idchar, which excludes CJK ideographs.

```catala
声明 作用域 A:
  输出 jia 内容 整数
  输出 yi 内容 布尔
  输出 bing 内容 金额

作用域 A:
  定义 jia 等于 4 - (2 - 2)
  定义 yi 等于 真
  定义 bing 等于 ¥1,234.56
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Typecheck --check-invariants
┌─[RESULT]─
│ All invariant checks passed
└─
┌─[RESULT]─
│ Typechecking successful!
└─
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope A
┌─[RESULT]─ A ─
│ jia = 4
│ yi = 真
│ bing = ¥1,234.56
└─
```

